3. Elementary Analytical Methods (p.1)
3.1. Binomial Theorem and Binomial Coefficients; Arithmetic and Geometric Progressions; Arithmetic, Geometric, Harmonic and Generalized Means
Binomial Theorem
(a+b)^{n}=a^{n}+\binom{n}{1}a^{n-1}b+\binom{n}{2}a^{n-2}b^{2}
+\binom{n}{3}a^{n-3}b^{3}+\ .\ .\ .+b^{n}
(n a positive integer)
Binomial Coefficients (see chapter 24)
3.1.2  \binom{n}{k}=nC_{x}=\frac{n(n-1)\cdot\ldots(n-k+1)}{k!}=\frac{n!}{(n-k)!k!}\]
3.1.3  \binom{n}{k}=\binom{n}{n-k}=(-1)^{x}\binom{k-n-1}{k}
3.1.4  \binom{n+1}{k}=\binom{n}{k}+\binom{n}{k-1}
3.1.5  \binom{n}{0}=\binom{n}{n}=1
3.1.6  1+\binom{n}{1}+\binom{n}{2}+\ .\ .+\binom{n}{n}=2^{n}
3.1.7  1-\binom{n}{1}+\binom{n}{2}-\ .\ .+(-1)^{n}\binom{n}{n}=0
